D, University of Arizona, 1992; MA, University of Auckland, 1988; BA, University of Auckland, 1985); Before joining ASU in 2006, she taught at the University of Auckland in New Zealand and University of Georgia. Alexandra Brewis Slade's research is concerned with how culture shapes human biology in the contexts of such massive, uncertain, and dynamic processes as climate change, growing social inequalities, urbanization, and globalization. Topically, she is focused on two fundamental, complex, and expanding problems related to the intersection of sustainability and health: obesity and water insecurity; publications: A. A. Brewis Slade, A. Brewis; Brewis, A.); viewed May 10, 2017 (publications include Obesity : cultural and biocultural perspectives (2011), Lives on the line (1996))uhttps://sustainability.asu.edu/person/alexandra-brewis-slade/  aLazy, crazy, and disgusting, 2019:bECIP title page (Alexandra Brewis) data view (birth date: April 13,1965)01002cz  a2200229n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040002600092100003300118400004000151400003400191400004100225400002800266670003500294670010200329670010500431670012400536670008700660675002500747nr 96021349 DLC19990526052733.1960610n| acannaab|          |a aaa     c  anr 96021349   aCtY-BRcCtY-BRdDLC-R1 aKugelmann, Louis,d1830-19021 aKugelʹman, L.q(Louis),d1830-19021 aKugelʹman, Louis,d1830-19021 aKugelmann,cDr.q(Louis),d1830-19021 aKūgeruman,d1830-1902  aPisʹma k L. Kugelʹmanu, 1907  aLouis Kugelmann, eine Biographie des Artzes und Freundes von Karl Marx und Friedrich Engels, 1974  aLC in RLIN, 13 June 1996b(hdg.: Kugelmann, Louis, 1830-1902; usage: Dr. Kugelmann, Louis Kugelmann)  aRLIN database, 13 June 1996b(hdg.: Kugelʹman, Louis, 1830-1902; usage: Louis Kugelmann, L. Kugelʹman, Dr. Kugelmann)  aKūgeruman e no tegami, 1926:bt.p. (in title: Kūgeruman [surname in katakana])  aDeutsche biog. Index00384cz  a2200133n  450000100130000000