bsolon at Wangford, where Mr. Torril, Mr. Blowgate, Mr. Brome, Mr. Lemon, and divers other gentlemen were drinking of healths. And the manner how the said thunderclaps rent and tore the house in divers places, striking divers of the aforesaid gentlemen lame, senseless, and carrying of Mr. Blowgate out of the parlour to the top of the room, and casting of him upon a table. As also, the striking of Mr. Torril dead, the hair of his head being almost all burnt of with the lightning, his legs somewhat bruised, and his head, face, and body, changed black. Attested by the fore-man of the jury, Mr. John Gibson, who on Thursday was sevennight was summoned upon the Crowners Quest, 1661.01447cz  a2200265n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040003800115046002100153100001800174373005000192373003500242374002000277375001900297377000800316378001700324670005900341670012500400670008300525670020400608670036900812nr 96025950 DLC20200701070530.0960717n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  anr 96025950   a(OCoLC)oca04136376  aCStbengerdacCStdNmUdDLCdICU  f1956-12-092edtf1 aKnapp, Sandra  aNatural History Museum (London, England)2naf  aLinnean Society of London2naf  aBotanists2lcsh  aFemales2lcdgt  aeng  qSandra Diane  aPsilotaceae a Salviniaceae, 1995:bt.p. (Sandra Knapp)  aOCLC, Apr. 26, 2004b(hdg.: Knapp, Sandra Diane; usage: Sandra Diane Knapp; author's Ph. D. thesis, Cornell Univ., 1986)  aBeyond cladistics, 2010:bECIP t.p. (Sandra Knapp) data view (b. Dec. 9, 1956)  aUnited Nations Environment Programme website, viewed March 31, 2010b(Dr.; Sandra Knapp; Dept. of Botany, came to the Natural History Museum, London, in 1992; studies plants of Central America, etc.)  aWikipedia, the free encyclopedia, June 30, 2020:bSandra Knapp (Sandra Diane Knapp FLS [Fellow of the Linnaean Society]; born 1965; American-born botranist; currently president of the Linnaean Society and a merit researcher of the P