re (Scotland)bBrighton (England)eLondon (England)  afacing Southampton Street, Stranda87 StrandaSloane StreetbLondondEngland  aBooksellers and booksellingaPublishers and publishing2lcsh  amale  aengafre1 wnneaaElmsley, Peter,d1734 or 5-18021 aElmsley, P.q(Peter),d1734 or 1735-18021 aElmsly, P.q(Peter),d1734 or 1735-18021 aElmsly, Peter,d1734 or 1735-18021 aElmesly,cM.,d1734 or 1735-1802  aCalonne, M. de. Abridgment of the memorial addressed to the King of France, 1787:bimprint on t.p. (P. Elmsley, Strand)  aEllis, J. The natural history of many curious and uncommon zoophytes, 1786:bimprint on t.p. (Peter Elmsly)  aDalrymple, A. A full and clear proof that Spaniards can have no claim to Balambangan, 1774:bimprint on t.p. (P. Elmsly, in the Strand)  aBailly, Jean Sylvain. Lettres sur l'origine des sciences, 1777:btitle page (A Londres : Chez M. Elmesly ; Et a Paris : Chez les freres Debure)  aPlomer, H.R. Dict. of the printers and booksellers 1726-1775, 1932b(Elmsley, Peter, bookseller and publisher in London, facing Southampton Street, Strand, 1770-6; d. May 3, 1802, aged 67)  aGentleman's magazine, May 1802, via HathiTrust, November 6, 2013:bpage (obituary: [died, May 3] at Brighthelmstone [Brighton] in the 67th year of his age, Peter Elmsly, esq., of Sloane-Street; a native of Aberdeenshire, and formerly a bookseller in the Strand; fine stylist in English and French)  aMaxted, Ian. Exeter working papers in book history. The London book trades 1775-1800, via WWW, November 6, 2013b(Elmsley, Peter, bookseller, Strand 1767-1802; Sloane Street, 1802; trading alone 1768-1797; as Elmsley and Bremner 1797-1802; born 1736, Aberdeenshire; died 3 May 1802 at Brighton in 67th year; importer of foreign books, often described as a French bookseller)uhttp://bookhistory.blogspot.com/2007/01/london-1775-1800-e.html  aDNB, via Oxford DNB, November 6, 2013b(Elmsley or Elmsly, Peter (1736-1802), bookseller, born in Aberdeenshire in 1736; died at Brighton, 3 May 1802, in his 67th year)  aOxford DNB, November 6, 2013b(Elmsley, Peter (1735/6-1802), bookseller; born in Aberdeenshire; partner with the bookseller Paul Vaillant, whose family had conducted a foreign bookselling business in the Strand, London, opposite Southampton Street, since 1686, but from 1768 Elmsley was trading there alone (from 1778 his address was 87 Strand); principally involved in importing foreign books and often described as a French bookseller; in 1797 Elmsley gave up his business to his shopman, David Bremmer; died at Brighthelmstone (Brighton) on 3 May 1802, in his 67th year)  aVIAF, November 6, 2013:bVIAF ID: 74082943 (Elmsley, Peter, 1736-1802: NUKAT Center (Poland), SUDOC (France), Bibliothèque nationale de France, Deutsche Nationalbibliothek; Elmsley, Peter, fl. 1736-1802: Biblioteca Nacional de España) VIAF ID: 14669824 (Elmsley, Peter, 1734 or 1735-1802: LC/NAF)00725cz  a2200217n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040004400115110002500159370001000184377000800194410003500202410002900237410002300266667005600289667004600345670011600391nr 96030123 DLC20120830074804.0960819n| azannaabn          |b ana        anr 96030123   a(OCoLC)oca04144906  aDLC-RbengerdacDLC-RdNNUdOCoLCdUPB2 aChiba-shi Bijutsukan  cJapan  ajpn1 aChiba-shi (Japan).bBijutsukan2 aChiba City Museum of Art2 a千葉市美術館  aMachine-derived non-Latin script reference project.  aNon-Latin script reference not evaluated.  aChiba-shi Bijutsukan shozō sakuhinsen, 1995:bt.p. (in title: Chiba-shi Bijutsukan; Chiba City Museum of Art)01189cz  a2200181n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002400115110005200139410005300191410004300244410004800287670016200335670051000497nr 96030127 DLC20130308073756.0960819n| acannaabn          |a ana     c  anr 96030127   a(OCoLC)oca04150107  aMWAbengcMWAdDNLM1 aBoston (Mass.).bBoa