kyo, Japan) is a Japanese manga artist and occasional musician ; graduated from Meisei University[1] with a degree in economics ; As a hobby Urasawa is also the vocalist and guitarist of a rock band. Under the stage name Bob Lennon, he wrote and performed the song "Kenji no Uta" ("Kenji's Song)" that was on a CD included in the first pressing of volume 11 of 20th Century Boys. He released his debut single "Tsuki ga Tottemo..." on June 4, 2008. and his debut album Half Century Man in 2009. In 2012 he performed a Japanese cover of Bob Dylan's "Girl from the North Country" and "Guta lala suda lala" from his series 20th Century Boys at the Japan Expo, and the following day he joined rock band Hemenway on stage.)00857cz  a2200229n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040003100115130002900146380005200175430003700227430004000264643003100304644001500335645002100350646001500371670011300386670012800499nr 96035377 DLC20210520064616.0961001n| azaabaaan          |a ana     c  anr 96035377   a(OCoLC)oca04288222  aPUbengerdacPUdDLCdUPB 0aArchitecture en Belgique  aSeries (Publications)aMonographic series2lcsh 0aSérie Architecture en Belgique 0aCollection Architecture en Belgique  aBruxellesbEditions Racine  af5DLC5PU  at5DPCC5DLC5PU  as5DLC5PU  aDierkens-Aubry, F. Le XIXe siècle en Belgique ... c1994:bt.p. verso (La série Architecture en Belgique)  aArt déco et modernisme en Belgique, c1996:bt.p. verso (Architecture en Belgique; La Collection Architecture en Belgique)00549cz  a2200181n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002900115100001700144400002800161400001400189667005600203667004600259670006200305nr 96035379 DLC20080910052520.0961001nc acannaabn          |b aaa        anr 96035379   a(OCoLC)oca04175051  aDLC-RbengcDLC-RdOCoLC1 aTao, Jingyun1 wnneaTʻao, Ching-yün1 a陶景云  aMachine-derived non-Latin script reference proje