University of Wisconsin--Madison)04049cz  a2200337n  nr 96040822 DLC20210114070125.0961113n| azannaabn          |a aaa     c  anr 96040822   a(OCoLC)oca04306800  aNjPbengerdacNjPdDLCdCaAEU  f1931-05-16g2019-05-202edtf1 aHolman, Derek,d1931-2019  cMember of the Order of Canadas2002t2019  aCornwall (England : County)bOttawa (Ont.)eToronto (Ont.)2naf  cEngland2naft1965  cCanada2nafs1965  aMusic2lcsh  aRoyal Academy of Music (London, England : 1822- )aUniversity of London2naf  aRoyal Army Educational Corps AssociationaRoyal School of Church Music (London, England)aUniversity of TorontoaSt. Paul's Cathedral (London, England)aCroydon Parish ChurchaCanadian Children's Opera Chorus2naf  aWestminster Abbey. Choir SchoolaBishop Strachan School (Toronto, Ont.)aGrace-Church-on-the-Hill (Toronto, Ont.)aChurch of St Simon the Apostle (Toronto, Ont.)aConcord Singers (Toronto, Ont.)aCroydon Bach Society  aRoyal Academy of Music (London, England : 1822- )aRoyal College of Organists (Great Britain)aRoyal School of Church Music (London, England)aCanadian Music CentreaCanadian League of ComposersaOrder of Canada2naf  aComposersaOrganistsaChurch musiciansaChoral conductors2lcsh  aMales2lcdgt1 wnneaaHolman, Derek,d1931-  aGlick, Holman, Somers, Coulthard, 1992:bcontainer (Derek Holman) insert (b. 1931)  aGrove music online WWW site, Dec. 19, 2014:b(Derek Holman; b. Redruth, Cornwall, 16 May 1931; English composer, organist and choral conductor; In 1965 he moved to Canada and became organist-choirmaster at Grace-Church-on-the-Hill (Toronto), a post he occupied until 1979)  aWikipedia, viewed 27 March 2020:bDerek Holman (choral conductor, organist and composer; born 16 May 1931, Illogan, Cornwall, England; attended the Royal Academy of Music from 1948 to 1952 and earned a Doctor of Music degree from the University of London; taught at the Royal Army Educational Corps from 1952 to 1954, the Westminster Abbey Choir School from 1954 to 1956, the Royal School of Church Music from 1956 to 1965, Bishop Strachan School from 1965 to 1970, and at the University of Toronto from 1966; organist at St Paul's Cathedral from 1956 to 1958, Croydon Parish Church from 1958 to 1965, Toronto's Grace Church on-the-Hill until 1979, and at Church of St Simon the Apostle from 1981 to 1998; directed the Concord Singers of Toronto from 1973 to 1975 and the Canadian Children's Opera Chorus from 1975 to 1985; founded the Croydon Bach Society in 1960; was a Fellow of the Royal Academy of Music, the Royal College of Organists, and the Royal School of Church Music, an associate of the Canadian Music Centre, and a member of the Canadian League of Composers; made a Member of the Order of Canada in 2002; died 20 May 2019, Ottawa, Ontario)  aCanada. Governor General. Honours Recipients database, 27 March 2020b(Derek Holman; Canada; Member of the Order of Canada, awarded on October 10, 2002, invested on May 9, 2003; He is a renowned choir director, composer and teacher. Numerous individuals and groups in the arts have commissioned his compositions. Recordings of his work have met with significant critical acclaim and live concerts and recitals have been presented throughout Canada. A professor of composition at the University of Toronto for nearly 30 years and now professor emeritus, he was regarded as a passionate and inspiring teacher who drew students from other musical disciplines and who taught several prominent Canadian composers. As a choirmaster, he was a mentor to countless young people in churches and in the Canadian Children's Opera Chorus.)  aCanadiana, viewed 27 March 2020b(authorized access point (0102C9182): Holman, Derek [Canadian, born 1931])00350nz  a2200121n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040001500092100003700107670008400144nr 96040823 DLC19970212064746.7961113n| acannaab|          |n aaa     c  anr 96040823   aNNFrcNNFr1 a