art2lcsh  aArtists2lcsh  aNot the same person as: Bacher, Lutz, 1941-  aDissent, difference and the body politic, 1993:bt.p. (Lutz Bacher) p. 21 (lives and works in Berkeley, Calif.; since mid-1970s, mostly use of appropriated texts, photos and video to examine gender roles, sexuality, reproduction)  aNew York times WWW site, viewed May 28, 2019b(in obituary published May 26: Lutz Bacher; d. May 14, Manhattan, aged 75; American Conceptual artist who, early in her career, adopted that fictional, masculine-sounding name and who thereafter refused to reveal personal details about her life; gave out a variety of birth dates over the years (the real one was Sept. 21, 1943), but did not say where she was born or provide any information about her family or educational background; all that was generally known was that she began making art in the San Francisco Bay Area in the 1970s, when Conceptualism had succeeded Minimalism as the influential new art movement; worked primarily with everyday found materials; in 2013, moved from Berkeley to New York City)  aWW in Amer. art, 1995/9600953cz  a2200217n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035001700092040003100109046001500140100005900155400004200214400005900256400005000315667009500365667003300460670007000493670017200563nr 97004904 DLC20120801110235.0970206n| acannaab           |a aaa     c  anr 97004904   a(Uk)tb710534  aESTC-NAbengcESTC-NAdDLC  f1745g17991 aDorset, John Frederick Sackville,cDuke of,d1745-17991 aSackville, John Frederick,d1745-17991 aSackville, John Frederick,cDuke of Dorset,d1745-17991 aSackville,cMr.q(John Frederick),d1745-1799  aTHIS 1XX FIELD CANNOT BE USED UNDER RDA UNTIL THIS RECORD HAS BEEN REVIEWED AND/OR UPDATED  aData provided by the ESTC/BL  aHis Poems by John Frederick Sackville, on various subjects, 1793.  aDNBb(Sackville, John Frederick, Duke of Dorset, b. 1745; elected member for Kent at the general election in 17