asbourg (in 1999))  aUniversité de Strasbourg website, 11 April 2017:bDépartement d'études arabes (M. Eric Geoffroy, MCF-HDR [maître de conférences-habilitation à diriger des recherches]; Université de Strasbourg; Faculté des langues et des cultures étrangères, Département d'études arabes; e-mail:e.geoffroy7@free.fr)  aWikipédia, l'encyclopédie libre, 11 April 2017b(Éric Geoffroy (Belfort, 1956); a French Arabist Islamologist and writer; teaches Islamology at the Université de Strasbourg and other institutions (Université ouverte de Catalogne, Université catholique de Louvain); academic specialist in Sufism and one of its major representatives in France; numerous travels in Arab countries; in 1984, converted to Islam, adopted the forename Younès; has taught Arabic and Islamic studies at Université de Strasbourg since 1995; also writes, lectures, and organises conferences on Islamic spirituality and culture, as well as on the challenges of spirituality in the modern world (globalization, postmodernism, ecology))01098cz  a2200217n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035001700092040003900109046002200148100003400170400003900204667003300243667003900276670033600315670003200651670011200683670008500795nr 97005423 DLC20130315133618.0970211n| azannaab           |a aaa     c  anr 97005423   a(Uk)tb037432  aUk/ESTC-NAbengerdacESTC-NAdDLC  f[1748,1749]2edtf1 aTrapp, Joseph,d1748 or 1749-1 wnneaaTrapp, Joseph,db. 1748 or 9  aData provided by the ESTC/BL  aCannot identify with Trapp, Joseph  aHis Proceedings of the French National Convention on the trial of Louis XVI. late King of France and Navarre; to which are added, several interesting occurrences and particulars ... the whole carefully collected from authentic documents, and republished with additions, from the paper of the World, 1793:bt.p. (Joseph Trapp, A.M.)  aNUC pre-56b(Trapp, Joseph)  aAlumni Oxon.:bser. 2 (Trapp, Joseph, s. J