ter Musical Festival2 aWorcester Three Choirs Festival  aData provided by the ESTC/BL  aIts The state of the charity, instituted in aid of the distribution annually made by the stewards of the meeting of the three choirs for the relief of the widows and orphans of clergymen in the diocese of Worcester: to Michaelmas, 1781, 1781.  aHunt, D. Elgar and the Three Choirs Festival, c1999:bt.p. (Three Choirs Festival) p. 7 ("The Three Choirs Festival is the popular name of what was known as the annual Music Meeting held in turn at the cathedrals of Gloucester, Hereford and Worcester. The date of the first festival is not known, but reference was made of its existence at Worcester in 1715, and this date is now commonly used as the starting point of the Festival's history ... From the earliest times there were collections to alleviate the poverty of widows and orphans of the clergy of the three dioceses;; the association with this charity continued until quite recently.")  aLysons, D. Origin and progress of the Meeting of the Three Choirs of Gloucester, Worcester & Hereford, and of the charity connected with it, 1895.  aThe Official Web Site of the Three Choirs Festivals, Jan. 14, 2004b(Worcester Three Choirs Festival; Hereford Three Choirs Festival; Gloucester Three Choirs Festival)  aWorcester Musical Festival, 1842bBL e-mail sent 24 Jan. 2008  aE-mail from Worcester Three Choirs Festival, 25 Jan. 2008b(According to our in-house historian, Michael Foster, the answer is The Worcester Music Festival was just another name given to the Three Choirs)  aThree Choirs Festival, WWW site, viewed June 19, 2017bHistory of the Three Choirs Festival (The origins of the annual Music Meetings of the Three Choirs of Gloucester, Worcester and Hereford were outlined in 1729 in a sermon preached by Thomas Bisse, Chancellor of Hereford Cathedral. His three-centuries-old words still serve to describe our festival today ... Hereford 2015, Celebration of the festival's 300th anniversary marked by performances of masterpieces of the repertoire from the three centuries including Beethoven Missa Solemnis, Verdi Requiem, The Dream of Gerontius, Bernstein Chichester Psalms.)00747cz  a2200169n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035001700092035002300109040003400132110003600166410003300202667003300235670030900268nr 97009873 DLC20080506072046.0970313n| acannaabn          |a ana     c  anr 97009873   a(Uk)tc090835  a(OCoLC)oca04294191  aUk/ESTC-NAbengcESTC-NAdOrU2 aW. Clarke and Son (Booksellers)2 aClarke and Son (Booksellers)  aData provided by the ESTC/BL  aIts A catalogue of books, comprising a variety of valuable, useful, and entertaining articles, in the various branches of ancient and modern literature, both new and second-hand. To which are added, a selection of the best modern publications, 1795:bt.p. (Which are now selling ... By W. Clarke and Son)00483cz  a2200157n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035001700092040004100109110003600150410003300186667003300219670007300252nr 97009874 DLC19970612052619.7970313n| acannaab|          |a ana     c  anr 97009874   a(Uk)tc010698  aUk/ESTC-NAcESTC-NAdESTC-NAdCtY-BR2 aW. Strahan and T. Cadell (Firm)2 aStrahan and T. Cadell (Firm)  aData provided by the ESTC/BL  aIts Books printed for W. Strahan, and T. Cadell in the Strand, 1772?00608nz  a2200145n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035001700092040002400109110005100133667003300184670024500217nr 97009883 DLC19970314052005.6970313n| acannaab|          |n ana     c  anr 97009883   a(Uk)tc000735  aUk/ESTC-NAcESTC-NA2 aWalker's New Coal Repository (London, England)  aData provided by the ESTC/BL  aIts The very best round coals. At Walker's New Coal Repository, Bell-Wharf, near Joiners-Hall, Dowgate, Upper Thames-Street. A real advantage of 3 shillings per chaldron, is saved by the purchasers of 