xt, by the grace of God Kyng of England, France, and Irelande, defender of the fayth, and in earthe, of the churche of England and also of Ireland, the supreme heade, nexte and immediatly vnder our sauioure Christ, 1550.  aDNBb(Ridley, Nicholas, 1500?-1555 (burnt at the stake); bishop of London, installed as Bonner's successor 1550; arrested and sent to the Tower of London, arrived 1553, and Bonner was at once reinstated bishop of London)00888nz  a2200157n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035001700092040002400109110007000133667003300203670038800236670010600624nr 97010179 DLC19970318051909.6970314n| acannaab|          |n ana     c  anr 97010179   a(Uk)sc094800  aUk/ESTC-NAcESTC-NA2 aChurch of England.bDiocese of London.bBishop (1611-1621 : King)  aData provided by the ESTC/BL  aIts Articles, to be enquired of vvithin the Dioces of London, in the second generall visitation of the right reuerend father in God, Iohn, Lord Bishop of London. Holden in the yeere of our Lord God 1615. In the thirteenth yeere of the reigne of our most gracious soueraigne lord Iames, by the grace of God, King of Great Britaine, France and Ireland, Defender of the Faith, &c, 1615.  aDNBb(King, John, DD, 1559?-1621; bishop of London, the bishopric bestowed upon him by the King 1611)00902nz  a2200157n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035001700092040002400109110007600133667003300209670038000242670012200622nr 97010181 DLC19970318051914.2970314n| acannaab|          |n ana     c  anr 97010181   a(Uk)sc094808  aUk/ESTC-NAcESTC-NA2 aChurch of England.bDiocese of Norwich.bBishop (1560-1575 : Parkhurst)  aData provided by the ESTC/BL  aIts Iniunctions exhibited by Iohn by gods sufferance Bishop of Norwich in his first visitacion beginning the seconde daie of Maye in the thirde yeare of our soueraign Ladie Elizabeth by the grace of God Quene of England, Fraunce and Ireland. Defendour of ye fait