 2017b(Olive Dungan (Pullen); Olive (Oliveca) Dungan was born in Pittsburgh in 1904; already a nationally know pianist by age 13, her family moved to Miami where she would become a major part of the Miami music scene for the next 80 years; during her long career, she would publish over 300 individual pieces of music; Dungan often wrote music in conjunction with others (as lyricist) including her husband, Charles Dungan, Mana-Zucca and even Vivian Laramore Rader, Florida's official poet laureate; Olive Dungan died in 1997)00576cz  a2200157n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040002600092046001500118100003900133374002200172670006400194670016000258nr 97010403 DLC20130109082752.0970317n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  anr 97010403   aPUbengerdacPUdDLC  f1881g19471 aDillon, Fannie Charles,d1881-1947  acomposerapianist  aAroma of the pines, c1927:bcaption (Fannie Charles Dillon)  aCohen, A.I. Intl. ency. of women composers, 1981b(Dillon, Fannie Charles; b. March 16, 1881, Denver; d. Feb. 21, 1947, Altadena, CA; pianist and composer)00443cz  a2200145n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040003000115100003200145400001900177670010100196nr 97010407 DLC20151204074005.0970317n| azannaabn          |a aaa     c  anr 97010407   a(OCoLC)oca04299497  aPUbengerdacPUdDLCdHU1 aSleeman, Antonia Petronella1 aSleeman, Petra  aLicensing empty nouns in French, c1996:bt.p. (Antonia Petronella Sleeman) cover (Petra Sleeman)00378nz  a2200133n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040001100092110002200103410004300125670007600168nr 97010421 DLC19970328051931.5970317n| acannaab|          |a ana     c  anr 97010421   aNNcNN2 aStift Dürnstein2 aAugustiner-Chorherrenstift Dürnstein  aStift Dürnstein, 1986:bp. 5 (Augustiner-Chorherrenstift Dürnstein)00817cz  a2200181n  450000100130000000300040001300500170001700800410003401000