naft1865  eCambridge (Mass.)2nafs18652 aJohn Wilson & Son2 aPress of John Wilson & Son2 wriPredecessor:aJohn Wilson (Firm: Boston, Mass.)  aThe Arabian nights entertainments, 1898:bverso of t.p. (John Wilson and Son; Cambridge, Mass., printer)  aEight cousins, 1875:bverso t.p. (John Wilson & Son)  aCoolidge, Susan. The New-Year's bargain, 1904:bverso of title-page (University Press: John Wilson & Son, Cambridge) page 231 (Cambridge: Press of John Wilson & Son)  aCambridge Historical Society, WWW site, viewed February 18, 2016 :bProceedings Volume 15, 1920-21, "Printing in Cambridge since 1800" by Norman Hill White, Jr., pages 21-22 (In 1865, immediately after Welch, Bigelow and Company removed from Holyoke Street [Cambridge], John Wilson and Son, printers, moved out from Boston. Here they printed from 1865 to 1879 when upon the failure of the firm of Welch, Bigelow and Company, the failing Company was bought out by John Wilson and Son together with Mr. Charles E. Wentworth. The entrance of Mr. Charles E. Wentworth did not change the firm name of John Wilson and Son. They took over the title sometimes used by Welch, Bigelow and Company of "The University Press." From 1879 until 1895 the printing establishment of John Wilson and Son printed successfully in Brattle Square for the College and for different publishers. In 1894 ...   John Wilson and Son failed ..... A corporation was formed with Mr. John Wilson as President and Mr. Henry White, President of the Cambridge Trust Company, as Treasurer. Through the interest and financial support of Henry White and Herbert H. White, his son, the corporation of John Wilson and Son, with the added name "The University Press" was formed)uhttp://www.cambridgehistory.org/content/printing-cambridge-1800  aCambridge Tribune, Volume XXVI, Number 11, May 16, 1903, viewed online on August 21, 2019:bentry for John Wilson dead (John Wilson established his business along with his father, also John Wilson, a printer, about fifty years ago, at 22 School street, Boston, under the firm name of John Wilson & Son)00722cz  a2200169n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040004000115100002100155375001900176378002000195670008800215670024900303nr 97010882 DLC20180406073319.0970320n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  anr 97010882   a(OCoLC)oca04300533  aNNFrbengerdacNNFrdMoSUdMdRoLAC1 aBooton, Diane E.  aFemales2lcdgt  qDiane Elizabeth  aPictorial seasons, 1994:bt.p. (Diane E. Booton) add. t.p. (Diane Elizabeth Booton)  aManuscripts, market and the transition to print in late Medieval Brittany, c2010:bt.p. (Diane E. Booton) p. i (Diane E. Booton, Ph. D., is an independent scholar specializing in the history of the book in late medieval and early modern Europe)00622nz  a2200145n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040001300092110006800105410006600173670011200239670012500351nr 97010885 DLC19970322052137.2970320n| acannaab|          |a ana     c  anr 97010885   aNICcNIC1 aUnited States.bForest Service.bSouthern Region.bGeometronics1 aUnited States.bForest Service.bGeometronics Southern Region  aEcological units of the eastern United States, 1995:bdisc label (prepared by Geometronics Southern Region)  aOCLC, 3/20/97b(hdg.: United States. Forest Service. Southern Region. Geometronics; usage: Geometronics Southern Region)00726nz  a2200157n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040002100092100003400113670007100147670011700218670009300335670014000428nr 97010893 DLC19970321051837.0970320n| acannaab|           n aaa     c  anr 97010893   aCaQMCCAcCaQMCCA1 aOhmann, Friedrich,d1858-1927  aFriedrich Ohmann's Entwürfe und ausgeführte Bauten, 1906-1914.  aMacmillan ency. of arch., c1982b(Ohmann, Friedrich; 1858-1927; b. Lemberg (now Lvov in the Ukraine); d. Vienna)  aThieme-Beckerb(Ohmann, Friedrich; architect; b. Lemberg 21.1