is)  aRodin, the Burghers of Calais, c2001:bt.p. (A. Haudiquet)  aAnnette Haudiquet, via WWW, September 27, 2017b(Annette Haudiquet has been the head of the Museum of Modern Art André Malraux since 2001; she previously headed the Museum of Fine Arts and Lace in Calais, where she developed an active policy of exhibitions on the nineteenth century--notably around the Societies of the Friends of the Arts or the figure of Rodin--on sculpture or on contemporary photography; in MuMa, she has curated extensive monographs (Raoul Dufy, Othon Friesz, Paul Signac, Camille Pissarro, Nicolas de Staël, Lyonel Feininger or Eugène Boudin) and thematic exhibitions (Waves, around the sea landscapes of Gustave Courbet, The clouds over there the wonderful clouds..); she completed the development of the Senn-Foulds donation and the publication of its catalog; she also co-curated the exhibition Le Cercle de l'art moderne. Avant-garde collectors at Le Havre, at the Luxembourg Museum in Paris in 2012)uhttp://www.uneteauhavre2017.fr/fr/annette-haudiquet00298nz  a2200121n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040001300092100001900105670005200124nr 97014488 DLC19970422051955.7970418n| acannaab|          |n aaa     c  anr 97014488   aNjPcNjP1 aGuzzo, Roberto  aL'inferno dei vivi, 1996:bt.p. (Roberto Guzzo)00562cz  a2200145n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040002800092100004000120400003600160670013100196670008900327nr 97014491 DLC20130829134005.0970418n| azannaab           |a aaa     c  anr 97014491   aNjPbengerdacNjPdDLC1 aGreenwood, G. W.q(Geoffrey Wilson)1 wnnaaGreenwood, Geoffrey Wilson  aCreep of engineering materials and of the Earth, 1978:bt.p. (G.W. Greenwood) p. 213 (Dept. of Metallurgy, Univ. of Sheffield)  aLC in RLIN, Apr. 15, 1997b(hdg.: Greenwood, Geoffrey Wilson; usage: G.W. Greenwood)00915nz  a2200205n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075