at Qatar Foundation Research and Development; he was also the inaugural Director of the Global Engineering Programs at Purdue University, West Lafayette, Indiana; his primary research is the development of a framework to quantify the linkages of the Water-Energy-Food Nexus that is constrained by climate change and social, political and technological pressures; he served on the World Economic Forum Global Agenda Council on Water Security, 2009-2011 (vice chair, 2011), Climate Change Agenda Council (2011- ), board of governors of the World Water Council (2012- ), advisory board of the UNFCC Momentum of Change Initiative (2012- ), advisory board of the President of the University of Alberta Water Initiative (2012- ) among many other global leadership roles)02992cz  a2200397n  nr 97016939 DLC20170511073820.0970508n| azannaabn          |a aaa     c  anr 97016939 7 aA940320082rid7 a195845922viaf7 a00000003235700682orcid7 a00000001212290052isni7 a000000013726346X2isni7 a70041460412scopus  a(OCoLC)oca04338340  aUPBbengerdacUPBdNmUdAuClMdInUdAuClM  f19542edtf1 aCawood, P. A.q(Peter Anthony),d1954-  cAustraliacScotlandeSt. Andrews (Scotland)2naf  aGeologyaGeochemistryaGeology, Structural2lcshvResearchGate website, viewed 24 May, 2016uhttps://www.researchgate.net/profile/Peter_Cawood  aMonash University2naf  aUniversity of St. Andrews. Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences.  aUniversity of Western Australia2naf  aGeologistsaCollege teachersaCollege department heads2lcsh  aResearcheraAcademic  amale  aeng  qPeter Anthony1 aCawood, Peter A.q(Peter Anthony),d1954-  aCurrent perspectives in the Appalachian-Caledonian orogen, 1995:bt.p. (P.A. Cawood; Sch. of Appl. Geol., Curtin Univ. of Tech., Perth, W. Australia) Can. CIP data on t.p. verso (Cawood, P. A. (Peter Anthony), 1954-) p. viii (Peter A. Cawood)  aOCLC database, 8/14/97b(hdgs: Cawood, P. A. (Peter Anthony), 1954- , and Cawood, P. A., and Cawood, Peter A.; usages: P.A. Cawood, Peter A. Cawood)  aMonash University/Medicine, Nursing and Health Sciences/News/2016 Researchers awarded Australian Laureate Fellowships website, viewed 24 May, 2016:b(Professor Peter Cawood's work ranges in scale from global reconstructions to microscopic examination of mineral grains. He is currently Chair in Geology and Head of the Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences at the University of St Andrews, Scotland. Through today's funding, Professor Cawood will lead a project at Monash that aims to establish the origin and evolution of the continental crust and its role in the long-term development of the Earth system)uhttp://www.med.monash.edu.au/news/2016/researchers-awarded-australian-laureate-fellowships.html  aCERSA website, viewed 24 May, 2016:b(Expertise: Structural geology and tectonics, Basin architecture, Field geology and mapping, Regional framework for mineral systems)uhttp://www.cersa.org.uk/p/98/prof-peter-cawood  aLaureate 2016 Bios Professor Peter Cawood, viewed 24 May, 2016:b(Current Organisation: The University of St Andrews, Scotland and The University of Western Australia. Administering Organisation, Monash University)uhttp://www.arc.gov.au/sites/default/files/filedepot/Public/Media%20&%20Resources%20Centre/Announcement%20Kits/May2016/FL16_Bios/PeterCawood_bio_web.docx00902cz  a2200205n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075035002300092040002800115046001500143100001600158370003400174374003900208377000800247670010700255670012400362670021000486nr 97016954 DLC20220317064546.0970508n| azannaabn          |n aaa     c  anr 97016954   a(OCoLC)oca04338345  aNjPbengerdacNjPdUPB  f19692edtf1 aAlary, Eric  aCosne-sur-Loire (France)2naf  aCollege teachersaHistorians2lcsh  afre  aLe canton de Bléré sous l'Occupation, 1994:bt.p. (Eric Alary) cover p. 4 (history prof. in Tours)  aHistoire des enfants, 2022:btitle page (Éric Al