NL  anlc  f19582edtf1 aKatz, Jonathan D.,d1958-  cGay men2lcdgt  aSaint Louis (Mo.)cUnited StatesfBuffalo (N.Y.)fNew Haven (Conn.)fSan Francisco (Calif.)fStony Brook (N.Y.)2naf  mjonathandavidkatz@gmail.com  aArt--HistoryaHomosexuality and artaGay artistsaGay and lesbian studies2lcsh  aState University of New York at Buffalo. Department of Art2naf  aYale University2naf  aLarry Kramer Initiative for Lesbian and Gay Studies  aCity College of San Francisco2naf  aState University of New York at Stony Brook2naf  aQueer Nation, San Francisco  aCollege teachersaArt historians2lcsh  amale  aMales2lcdgt  aeng  qJonathan David1 aKatz, Jonathan David,d1958-1 aKatz, Jonathan,d1958-1 wnneaaKatz, Jonathanq(Jonathan D.)2 wriFounded corporate body:aHarvey Milk Institute2 wriFounded corporate body:aCollege Art Association of America.bGay and Lesbian Caucus2 wriFounded corporate body:aAnnual National Queer Arts Festival  aAndy Warhol, 1993:bt.p. (Jonathan Katz)  aExcite people finder, Apr. 26, 1997b(Katz, Jonatha[n] D.; San Francisco)  aCorresp. from J. Katz, May 9, 1997b(author of Andy Warhol; not Jonathan Ned Katz; not author of works on art grants; founder and chair of Harvey Milk Institute in San Francisco)  aRLIN, Nov. 1, 2000b(hdg.: Katz, Jonathan David, 1958- )  aDifference/indifference, c1998:bt.p. (Jonathan D. Katz) front flap (Ph. D., art hist., Northwestern Univ.)  aYale database, Feb. 18, 2005b(Jonathan D. Katz directs the Larry Kramer Initiative for Lesbian and Gay Studies at Yale University)  aArt AIDS America, 2015:btitle page (Jonathan David Katz) page 286 (Director, Visual Studies Doctoral Program, University at Buffalo, The State University of New York)  aWikipedia, January 20, 2016b(Jonathan David Katz (born 1958) is an American activist, art historian, educator and writer, he is currently the director of the doctoral program in Visual culture studies at State University of New York at Buffalo. He is also the former executive coordinator of the Larry Kramer Initiative for Lesbian and Gay Studies at Yale University. He is a former chair of the Department of Lesbian and Gay Studies at the City College of San Francisco, and was the first tenured faculty in gay and lesbian studies in the United States. Katz was an associate professor in the Art History Department at the State University of New York at Stony Brook, where he also taught queer studies; founder of the Harvey Milk Institute and the Queer Caucus for Art of the College Art Association; co-founded Queer Nation San Francisco; born St. Louis, Missouri)  aHis resume, via Queer Cultural Center website, January 20, 2016b(Jonathan Katz; Jonathan D. Katz Ph.D.; 1991-1999: Chair, Department Of Gay, Lesbian and Bisexual Studies, City College of San Francisco; 1999-2000: Visiting Associate Professor, University of Amsterdam; 2001-2002: Associate Professor, Department of Art, SUNY, Stony Brook; 2002-2006: Founding Director, Lesbian and Gay Studies; Associate Prof. History of Art & Women, Gender And Sexuality Studies--Yale University; 2006-2012  Guest curator, National Portrait Gallery, Smithsonian Institution; 2008-2011: Honorary Research Fellow, University of Manchester, UK, Faculty of the Humanities; 2010- : Chair, Visual Studies Doctoral Program, SUNY, Buffalo; 1989: Founder and inaugural chair, Gay and Lesbian Caucus, College Art Association; 1990: Co-Founder, Queer Nation, San Francisco; 1994: Founder and Chair, The Harvey Milk Institute; 1998: Founding artistic Director, National Queer Arts Festival, San Francisco)uhttp://www.queerculturalcenter.org/Pages/KatzPages/KatzBio.html  aOCLC, January 20, 2016b(access point: Katz, Jonathan (Jonathan D.); usage: Jonathan D. Katz; Jonathan David Katz; Jonathan Katz)  aUniversity at Buffalo Department of Art website, January 20, 2016b(Jonathan Katz; Associate Professor, Department Chair, Director, PhD Program; Jonathan D. Katz works at the intersection of art history and queer history; a specialist in the arts of the Cold War era, he is centrally concerned with the question of why the American avant-garde came to be dominated and defined by queer artists during what was perhaps the single most homophobic decade in this nation's history)uhttp://art.buffalo.edu/people/full-time-faculty/jonathan-katz/  aUB online directory, January 20, 2016b(Jonathan D Katz; Director, Visual Studies Doctoral Program; Associate Professor; jonathandavidkatz@gmail.com)00361nz  a2200121n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040001300092100002000105670011400125nr 97018178 DLC19970520071600.5970519n| acannaab|          |n aaa     c  anr 97018178   aNICcNIC1 aDiehl, Susan V.  aBioremediation of low level PCP and PAHs contaminated water using biofiltration, 1996:bt.p. (Susan V. Diehl)00450cz  a2200133n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040001800092100002700110670007200137670010700209nr 97018193 DLC20041026171957.0970519n| acannaab           |n aaa     c  anr 97018193   aNICcNICdDLC1 aÓ Dochartaigh, Niall  aFrom civil rights to armalites, 1997:bt.p. (Niall Ó Dochartaigh)  aFrom civil rights to armalites, 2005:bCIP t.p. (Niall Ó Dochartaigh) data sheet (b. Sept. 16, 1966)00610cz  a2200145n  4500001001300000003000400013005001700017008004100034010001700075040001800092100001600110400002100126670018700147670013000334nr 97018197 DLC19990319140331.0970519n| acannaab|          |a aaa     c  anr 97018197   aNjPcNjPdDLC1 aChau, F. S.1 aChau, Fook Siong  aInternational Conference on Experimental Mechanics: Advances and Applications, c1997:bt.p. (F.S. Chau) p. 597 (Dept. of Mechanical & Production Engineering, Nat. Univ. of Singapore)  aSirohi, R.S. Optical methods of measurement, 1999:bCIP t.p. (Fook Siong Chau, Nat. Univ. Singapore) data sheet (b. 04/05/52)00881cz  a2200217n  4500001001300000003000400